@* Tabs (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/navigation.css</code></li>
    <li>Behaviour <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/wwwroot/dnf.js</code> (<code>[data-tabs]</code>)</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>Tabs show the panels of one screen one at a time. Write a <code>[data-tabs]</code> root with a
    <code>dnf-tabs</code> tab list and one <code>dnf-tab-panel</code> per tab; <code>dnf.js</code> does the rest. Without
    JavaScript every panel shows, one below the other, each with its title - so the content stays readable.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="tabs" layout="block">
    <div data-tabs data-initial-tab="general">
        <div class="dnf-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Page settings">
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="tabs-general-tab" aria-controls="tabs-general-panel" data-tab="general">General</button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="tabs-seo-tab" aria-controls="tabs-seo-panel" data-tab="seo">SEO</button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="tabs-access-tab" aria-controls="tabs-access-panel" data-tab="access">Access</button>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="tabs-general-panel" aria-labelledby="tabs-general-tab" data-tab-panel="general">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">General</h3>
            <p>The page's title, slug and parent in the page tree.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="tabs-seo-panel" aria-labelledby="tabs-seo-tab" data-tab-panel="seo">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">SEO</h3>
            <p>The meta title and description search engines show, and whether the page is indexed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="tabs-access-panel" aria-labelledby="tabs-access-tab" data-tab-panel="access">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">Access</h3>
            <p>Who can see the page: everyone, signed-in users, or some roles only.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="with-badges" title="With badges" description="A badge in a tab counts what is inside (problems, items). data-tab-hash false keeps this group out of the URL." layout="block">
    <div data-tabs data-initial-tab="fields" data-tab-hash="false">
        <div class="dnf-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Content type">
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="badges-fields-tab" aria-controls="badges-fields-panel" data-tab="fields">Fields <span class="dnf-badge">8</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="badges-entries-tab" aria-controls="badges-entries-panel" data-tab="entries">Entries <span class="dnf-badge">124</span></button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-tabs__tab" role="tab" id="badges-problems-tab" aria-controls="badges-problems-panel" data-tab="problems">Problems <span class="dnf-badge dnf-badge--danger">2</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="badges-fields-panel" aria-labelledby="badges-fields-tab" data-tab-panel="fields">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">Fields</h3>
            <p>Title, slug, summary, body, cover image, author, tags and publish date.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="badges-entries-panel" aria-labelledby="badges-entries-tab" data-tab-panel="entries">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">Entries</h3>
            <p>124 entries use this content type.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-tab-panel pt-4" role="tabpanel" id="badges-problems-panel" aria-labelledby="badges-problems-tab" data-tab-panel="problems">
            <h3 class="dnf-tab-panel__title">Problems</h3>
            <p>Two entries have no cover image although the field is required.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="links" title="Tabs between screens" description="Links in a nav.dnf-tabs switch between screens; the current one has aria-current page. No tab roles and no data-tabs - this is navigation." layout="block">
