<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-tabs</code></td><td>block</td><td>a horizontally scrolling row with a 1px line below (an inset shadow)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-tabs__tab</code></td><td>element</td><td>muted semibold text with a 2px bottom border; a badge inside is 1.2rem high</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-tab-panel</code></td><td>block</td><td>a column, gap <code>--dnf-space-4</code>; consecutive panels separated by a line (without JS)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-tab-panel__title</code></td><td>element</td><td><code>text-md</code> semibold - visible without JS, visually hidden (<code>sr-only</code>) once tabbed</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3 id="states">States</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>State</th><th>Selector</th><th>Look</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>selected / current</td><td><code>[aria-selected="true"]</code>, <code>[aria-current="page"]</code></td><td>foreground text, <code>--dnf-primary</code> underline</td></tr>
        <tr><td>hover</td><td><code>:hover</code></td><td>foreground text</td></tr>
        <tr><td>keyboard focus</td><td><code>:focus-visible</code></td><td>2px focus outline inside the tab</td></tr>
        <tr><td>tabbed</td><td><code>[data-tabbed="true"]</code> on the root</td><td>one panel at a time, no separators, panel titles visually hidden</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There is no tag helper: the classes and these hooks are the API.</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>[data-tabs]</code></td><td>the root; gets <code>data-tabbed="true"</code>. It manages only its own tabs and panels - a panel may hold another tab group</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-tab="name"]</code></td><td>a tab; gets <code>aria-selected</code> and a roving <code>tabindex</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-tab-panel="name"]</code></td><td>its panel; the others get <code>hidden</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-initial-tab="name"</code></td><td>the first tab when the URL hash names none (else the first tab)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-tab-hash="false"</code></td><td>neither reads nor writes the URL hash (several small tab groups on one page)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-tab-field]</code></td><td>a form field that receives the open tab's name</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>By default the open tab is written to the URL hash (<code>#seo</code>, with <code>history.replaceState</code>), so a reload or a
    redirect to <code>…#seo</code> reopens it; a <code>hashchange</code> switches too.</p>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>With JS: <code>role="tablist"</code> / <code>tab</code> / <code>tabpanel</code>, <code>aria-selected</code> and a roving
        <code>tabindex</code>; ArrowLeft and ArrowRight (wrapping), Home and End move between tabs.</li>
    <li>Tie tabs and panels together with <code>aria-controls</code> and <code>aria-labelledby</code> in the markup, and name the
        tab list with <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
    <li>Without JS every panel shows with its title as a heading; once tabbed the title stays for screen readers only.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use the URL hash (<code>/admin/pages/7#seo</code>) to redirect back to the tab a form was saved from.</li>
    <li>Do keep tab names short - one or two words.</li>
    <li>Don't put the tab roles on link tabs between screens - they are navigation (<code>aria-current="page"</code>).</li>
    <li>Don't use tabs for a small exclusive choice like a filter - that is a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/segmented">segmented control</a>.</li>
</ul>
